  "name": "Question 8",
  "problem": "The vector $u$ has magnitude $5$, the vector $v$ has magnitude $4,$ the angle between $u$ and $v$ is ${160}^{\u2218}$ and $n$ is the unit vector that points in the direction of $u\\times v.$ Find $u\\times v$ in terms of $n.$ Round your final answer to one decimal place where appropriate.",
  "worked_solution": "We use the formula for the cross product and obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\times v & =|u|\\cdot |v|\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta \\cdot n \\\\  & =5\\cdot 4\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}\u2061{160}^{\u2218}\\cdot n \\\\  & =20\\cdot (0.342\\,02\u2026)\\cdot n \\\\  & =(6.840\\,40\u2026)\\cdot n \\\\  & \u22486.8n.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
